Subject: [PATCH] rpmsg: glink: avoid recursive device removal during detach

Backport of upstream 5a5a48e788e02fd8a8eb7188ce440572d6c12418
(stable 7.2.y: e559626bee8a6632aafc08eedcdb4bf26ca245c5).
Upstream authors: Deepak Kumar Singh and Vishnu Santhosh, Qualcomm.

The device core holds the device mutex while detaching a driver. Removing
that device again from endpoint teardown deadlocks module removal and can
block shutdown. Channel-close handlers already unregister the device.

Observed while removing the temporary charger-log reader on houji.
This changes teardown only; it does not change charging policy.

--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c
@@ -1418,9 +1418,6 @@
 	channel->ept.cb = NULL;
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&channel->recv_lock, flags);
 
-	/* Decouple the potential rpdev from the channel */
-	qcom_glink_remove_rpmsg_device(glink, channel);
-
 	qcom_glink_send_close_req(glink, channel);
 }
 
